In article <THOTH.90Sep15221739@reef.cis.ufl.edu> thoth@reef.cis.ufl.edu (Gilligan) writes:

>   Well, has anyone noticed the release of color xterm?

>   It accepts a few escape sequences to set the foreground and
> background colors to any combination from 8 colors: black, red, green,
> yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, and white.  If the user doesn't like red
> being red he can change it to forestgreen (the wonders of X windows:).

>   So my question is "does nethack already support this?".  I hear
> legends that it supports PC ansi.sys or whatever and I wonder if color
> xterm is compatible.

>   Please answer by mail since I read comp.windows.x and therefore have
> no time to read other groups:) I'll be glad to answer questions about
> the specific escape sequences if necessary.
> --
> #!perl -ne
> #/--------------------
